🎨 Always use colors from the design token system to maintain consistency.

4. Typography

Primary Font: Inter, sans-serif

Font Sizes:

Heading 1 → 32px / Bold

Heading 2 → 24px / Semi-Bold

Body → 16px / Regular

Caption → 12px / Regular

Line Height: 1.5

Letter Spacing: Normal

Avoid using custom font weights not part of the defined scale.

5. Component Guidelines
Buttons

Primary Button: Solid background using the primary color, white text.

Secondary Button: Transparent background, bordered with primary color.

Disabled State: Reduced opacity and non-interactive cursor.

Forms

Use rounded corners (border-radius: 8px).

Always include label + helper text.

Show validation messages in red (#DC2626).

Cards

Shadow: 0 4px 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)

Border radius: 12px

Padding: 16px

6. Code Formatting Rules

Language: TypeScript (preferred)

Linting: ESLint + Prettier

Indentation: 2 spaces

Naming conventions:

Variables: camelCase

Components: PascalCase

Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE

Imports: Group and order by external → internal → relative paths.

Comments: Use // for single-line and /** */ for function or class documentation.

7. Git and Repository Standards

Branch Naming Convention:

feature/<name> → for new features

fix/<name> → for bug fixes

hotfix/<name> → for urgent production fixes

docs/<name> → for documentation changes

Commit Message Format:

<type>(scope): short description


Example:

feat(auth): add JWT-based authentication
fix(ui): resolve header alignment issue
docs(style-guide): update typography section


Pull Request Checklist:

Code linted and formatted

All tests passing

Updated documentation if applicable

8. Accessibility & Responsiveness

Use semantic HTML elements.

Ensure contrast ratios meet WCAG standards.

Components should be fully responsive from 320px (mobile) to 1440px+ (desktop).

9. Image & Icon Usage

Use SVGs for all icons.

Optimize images using TinyPNG or ImageOptim before committing.

Store reusable images in /assets/images/.

10. Version Control

All code changes must go through PR reviews.

Do not commit generated or build files (dist/, node_modules/).

Tag releases following semantic versioning:

v<major>.<minor>.<patch>

